    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;4.08</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Clinical, laboratory, histological, and genetic features suggestive&nbsp;of autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome (ALPS) and ALPS-like disorders</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Haematolymphoid tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2024. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 11). https://publications.iarc.who.int/637.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 769px; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.8906px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"10%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Features</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">ALPS</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Overlap</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 209.984px; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">ALPS-like</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.8906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"10%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Autoimmune cytopenia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Risk of malignancy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Autoimmune cytopenia</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Risk of malignancy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 209.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">Frequent: recurrent infections, enteropathy, skin lesions</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Infrequent: HLH, arthritis, neurological symptoms, endocrinopathy and cardiomyopathy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.8906px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"10%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Laboratory</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Increased:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>CD3+ TCR&alpha;&beta;+ CD4&minus; CD8&minus; T&nbsp;cells (DNT cells)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Vitamin&nbsp;B12, sFASL, IL-10</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span lang=\"FR\" style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-ansi-language: FR;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Ig<span lang=\"FR\">G</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span lang=\"FR\">Normal:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>IgG antibody responses</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Decreased:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>FAS-induced apoptosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 16px;\">Antipolysaccharide IgM response in active disease</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 12pt; text-indent: -12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Memory B-cell lymphopenia</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 209.984px; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">Variable DNT cells, vitamin&nbsp;B12, sFASL, IL-10</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Variable IgG, IgM</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Specific alteration of T, B, and/or NK cells</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Normal FAS-induced apoptosis except in STAT3 GOF and deficiencies of LRBA and TET2</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.8906px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"10%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histological</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Paracortical expansion with DNT cells in lymph nodes, spleen, and occasionally extranodal sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymphoid infiltrates at extranodal sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 209.984px; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Lymphocytic infiltration of non-lymphoid organs including gut, lung, and brain (especially in LRBA and CTLA-4 defects)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.8906px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"10%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Genetic</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Germline mutations: <em>FAS</em>, <em>FASLG</em>, <em>FADD</em>, <em>CASP10</em>, and <em>CASP8</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Somatic mutations: <em>FAS</em></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 210.312px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">None</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 209.984px; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"29%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Immune dysregulation (EBV susceptibility): <em>PRKCD</em>, <em>MAGT1</em>, <em>XIAP</em>, <em>SH2D1A</em>, <em>RASGRP1</em>, <em>TNFRSF9</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"FR\">Immune dysregulation (Treg defect): <em>STAT3</em>, <em>CTLA4</em>, <em>LRBA</em>, <em>IL2RA</em>, <em>IL2RB</em>, <em>DEF6</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Antibody deficiencies: <em>PIK3CD</em> and <em>CARD11</em> GOF, <em>PIK3R1</em> LOF</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Combined immunodeficiency: <em>ITK</em>, <em>STK4</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Defects in innate immunity: <em>STAT1</em> GOF, <em>IL12RB1</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Autoinflammatory disorders: <em>ADA2</em>, <em>TNFAIP3</em>, <em>TET2</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; text-indent: 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Phenocopies of IEI: somatic mutations in <em>NRAS</em>, <em>KRAS</em> <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{31953710;33598806}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">DNT cell, double-negative T&nbsp;cell; GOF, gain of function; HLH, haemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis; IEI, inborn error of immunity; LOF, loss of function; Treg, regulatory T&nbsp;cell.</span></p>",
